getting close to our Paleolithic  ancestors has helped to give svante  herbo his moment in history  the Swedish geneticist was handed  flowers and received congratulations  from his colleagues at the Max Planck  Institute in Leipzig Germany after being  named the 113th Nobel Prize winner in  physiology or medicine in his hometown  of Stockholm well under many years this  is my first thought was that this was a  sophisticated joke by my colleagues but  then it sounded a little too convincing  so I accepted that it was true it's  particularly fulfilling because it  started as a hobby doing something I  loved 30 years ago and for a long time  this research was seen as a bit of a  curiosity and now I think it's really  arrived as a serious research topic with  many different groups now working on it  purbo is credited with transforming the  study of human Origins he pioneered the  examination of DNA sequences from  archaeological and paleontological  remains to bridge the gap between  ourselves as Homo sapiens and our  extinct ancestors the Neanderthals  because of his discoveries we're able to  understand what makes us different and  unique from these close relatives  neanderthals were living in Europe over  a half a million years ago we Homo  sapiens came out of Africa about 75 000  years ago we mixed with neanderthals in  the Middle East we now know that we Homo  sapiens carry about one to two percent  of DNA from neanderthals we know that  from his work not content with bringing  neanderthals into the present purbo also  discovered another even older race the  Denise Evans thanks to DNA from a 40 000  year old bone found in a cave in Siberia  perbo's discovery of the denisovans then  led to evidence that they had mixed with  neanderthals Pebble was then able to  show that there's a little bit of  denisovan in all of us as well how about  seems to be the beneficiary of good  genes himself his father Suna Bergstrom  won a Nobel Prize in medicine in 1982.  what this Swedish scientist passes on to  the next generation is a better  understanding of the generations that  came a very long time before  Al Jazeera Stockholm
 

